    <briefdescription>
<para>Cash flow dependent on an index ratio. </para>    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>This cash flow is not a coupon, i.e., there&apos;s no accrual. The amount is either i(T)/i(0) or i(T)/i(0) - 1, depending on the growthOnly parameter.</para><para>We expect this to be used inside an instrument that does all the date adjustment etc., so this takes just dates and does not change them. growthOnly = false means i(T)/i(0), which is a bond-type setting. growthOnly = true means i(T)/i(0) - 1, which is a swap-type setting. </para>    </detaileddescription>
